   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ordinary people who never become famous can still shape history.","is_correct":true},{"text":"History projects should never be about presidents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Floods were the most important events of the 1800s.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Ferries are more useful than bridges for crossing rivers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ordinary people who never become famous can still shape history.$q$, $q$Eliza Brandt is in no textbook, yet her fourteen trips saved families during the flood. The story does not say presidents are bad topics, only that ordinary people matter too.$q$, 'draft', '2f954d15-ec7a-5df8-b727-69a5cf23e2c3')
